# 🤖 AI Company Agent Platform Rules

You are a Senior AI Engineer building a production-grade Multi-Agent AI Platform.

## Project Stack

- Python 3.12
- FastAPI
- Streamlit
- LangGraph
- LiteLLM
- SQLite
- Qdrant
- HuggingFace Embeddings
- Groq API
- OpenRouter API

## AI Model Rules

Never use:
- OpenAI API
- Anthropic API
- Gemini API

Always route LLMs through LiteLLM.

### Planner
DeepSeek V3 via OpenRouter.

### Coding
Qwen Coder via Groq.

### Reasoning
Llama 3.3 70B via Groq.

### Vision
Llama Vision via Groq.

### Embeddings
BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 using sentence-transformers.

## Architecture Rules

This project follows modular architecture.

backend/
    agents/
    api/
    graph/
    memory/
    models/
    prompts/
    rag/
    tools/
    utils/

frontend/
    pages/
    components/

## Agent Rules

Each AI agent must live in its own file.

Example:

agents/
    planner_agent.py
    research_agent.py
    coder_agent.py
    reviewer_agent.py
    database_agent.py
    memory_agent.py
    vision_agent.py
    qa_agent.py

Each agent must have:

- System prompt.
- execute() function.
- Pydantic response model.
- Logging.

## Prompt Rules

Never hardcode long prompts inside Python.

Store prompts inside:

backend/prompts/

One prompt file per agent.

## Memory Rules

Short-term memory:

SQLite.

Long-term memory:

Qdrant Vector Database.

Never mix business logic with memory logic.

## RAG Rules

Pipeline order:

Document
→ Chunk
→ Embed
→ Store
→ Retrieve
→ Inject Context
→ LLM

Chunk size configurable.

Embeddings stored in Qdrant.

## API Rules

Use async FastAPI routes.

Return Pydantic models.

Never return raw dictionaries from API endpoints.

## Streamlit Rules

Frontend contains UI only.

Do not place AI logic inside Streamlit pages.

Call FastAPI endpoints.

## Security Rules

Never commit:

.env
API Keys
SQLite databases
Qdrant storage
Logs

Always use environment variables.

## Code Quality

- Type hints everywhere.
- Google-style docstrings.
- Logging instead of print().
- Modular reusable functions.
- No duplicate code.
- Follow PEP8.

## Git Rules

Every feature should be committed separately.

Example commits:

feat(planner): add CEO planner agent
feat(memory): add sqlite memory
feat(rag): implement qdrant retrieval
feat(ui): add streamlit dashboard
fix(api): resolve router bug

## Documentation Rules

Every module needs:

- Purpose.
- Inputs.
- Outputs.
- Example usage.

README must stay updated with new features.

## Testing Rules

Every major module gets a test inside:

tests/

Use pytest-compatible structure.

## Future Expansion

Architecture should support:

- Voice Agent
- Vision Agent
- Email Agent
- WhatsApp Agent
- GitHub Agent
- Calendar Agent
- Deployment Agent
- MCP Tool Integration

Always keep the project scalable.